# =============================================================================
# BEGINNER GUIDE TO THIS SNAKEFILE (first 1397 lines)
#
# What this workflow does overall:
# 1. Read a profile-specific config (for example: heme, nbl, rbl, brca, pan_cancer).
# 2. Build feature/gene sets from a joint expression matrix.
# 3. Run many unsupervised clustering jobs across method × distance combinations.
# 4. Build consensus clustering summaries from those clustering results.
# 5. Build tumour-neighbourhood inputs and run tumour-neighbourhood analysis.
#
# How to read this file as a beginner:
# - 'input:' means files a rule needs.
# - 'output:' means files a rule creates.
# - 'params:' means extra settings passed to scripts.
# - 'log:' is where stdout/stderr are written.
# - 'conda:' selects the software environment for that rule.
# - Most heavy work is actually done by the R scripts in scripts/.
# - The Snakefile's job is to connect those scripts into a reproducible DAG.
# =============================================================================

